    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d201">

                <pb facs="0300" n="226" xml:id="pg226"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/633</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Moscow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Summers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-08T16:00:00+03:31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 8, 1917, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received November 10, 6.10
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>53. Revolutionary party headed by Council of Workmen-Soldiers’ Deputies supported
                    by garrison have taken over government of Moscow including administration post,
                    telegraph. They have closed offices of all conservative newspapers. All
                    relatively quiet. Consulate General will keep the Department fully informed and
                    will take all necessary steps to protect American citizens and their
                    interests.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Summers</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
